WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.036
Controversial New York congressman,

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:03.670
Republican George

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.237
Santos, now

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.472
officially under investigation

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:06.840
by the House Ethics Committee.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.575
It will look into multiple issues

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.143
from his campaign finances

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.145
to a sexual misconduct allegations.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.480
Our great reporters are back

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.482
and Santos is now infamous

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.516
for just lying and lying

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.851
and lying and lying.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.552
But the substance of these allegations

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.253
are quite serious.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.755
The committee has acknowledged

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:22.889
its investigation

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.557
potential unlawful activity

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.192
by his 2022 campaign,

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.293
potential violations

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.029
of federal conflict of interest

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:29.729
laws for work

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:30.363
he did

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.266
for a firm providing fiduciary services.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:33.800
He may have failed

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.268
to disclose information

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.936
on his statements filed with the House

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:39.005
and the sexual misconduct allegation

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.006
that he made

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.241
an inappropriate advance toward

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:42.876
someone seeking a job in his office.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.445
So America knows Jorge Santos is a liar.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.780
That's a serious list.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.381
Yeah, it is a serious lesson.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.983
George Henderson says

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.518
House career is hanging by a thread.

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:53.553
And it is this,

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:53.853
you know,

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.488
typically the House Ethics Committee,

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.322
Senate Ethics Committee,

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.624
they do these investigations.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.092
It's a slap on the wrist.

00:00:59.092 --> 00:00:59.993
They get admonished.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:00.860
No one cares.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.995
This is different

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.263
because not only is the scope

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.497
very, very serious,

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.266
but the Republican leadership.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.435
Kevin McCarthy has now staked

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.737
Santos his career on the outcome of this.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.772
At the promise of that time and again,

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:13.940
as I've pressed him on this,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.841
others have pressed him on this.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.009
He's now pointing that,

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:18.178
as he says, if they find any wrongdoing,

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.546
that's when they could push him out.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:20.547
And how do you push him out?

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.515
An expulsion resolution in the House

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:23.983
requires two thirds majority.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.851
Kevin McCarthy

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.486
gets behind the expulsion

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.787
resolution of Jorge Santos.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:28.521
He is done

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:29.389
he's not going to be a House

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.223
member anymore.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.057
That's what is.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.058
But the question is,

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.760
if you go through that serious list,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.261
how House Ethics Committees

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.896
and I'll get to another one in a minute.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:37.530
These investigations

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.498
tend to go on forever.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.833
And ever and ever and ever.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.101
So does Kevin McCarthy.

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:41.401
You know,

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.902
does he want to get his wish,

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.636
but not right away

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.472
because he needs Jorge Santos, his vote?

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:45.839
Well,

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.841
he does continue to need Jorge Santos.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.542
His vote it's a math problem.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.810
I recently did a story

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.946
about shamelessness

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.647
in American politics in this new age.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.716
Long story. And it was a long story.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:57.517
And I working

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.251
and I interviewed

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.019
former Congressman Anthony Weiner,

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.488
who left in a cloud of shame.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.156
One thing he told me that I think

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:03.857
is relevant

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.792
to the Santos situation is

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.128
it wasn't just the reporters hounding him

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.662
It wasn't just his colleagues

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.029
telling him

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.364
they didn't want to be seen with him.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.599
It was also that he was facing

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.134
hundreds of thousands of dollars

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.035
in legal fees to actually properly

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.203
defend himself

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.339
against a house ethics investigation.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:22.108
So is this another weight on the scale

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.843
for Santos?

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.377
Who knows?

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.412
But I do know that in that case,

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.347
there was

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:28.715
the ethics

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:29.616
investigation wasn't

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.618
just that it would take forever, and

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.653
but that it would be expensive to defend.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.622
And especially the New York

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.623
the other New York freshman

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.357
who came in with him

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.658
that's why Kevin McCarthy is speaker.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.926
They flipped all these seats in New York,

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:40.793
Michael, all.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.163
As I've said before, Jorge Santos conduct

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:43.830
his conduct

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.064
is embarrassing and unbecoming.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.133
If he had any dignity, he would resign

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.035
Your point is a potential question down

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.570
the road. This has become too expensive.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.337
But at the moment,

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.772
he seems to think staying

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.007
is how you raise that money

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:54.841
for the legal fees.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.675
That's right. That's right.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:59.312
And even just as well, while he stays,

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.381
even if this report is delayed

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.015
and the Ethics

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.249
Committee investigation

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.551
does go on for a while,

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:05.785
we were talking about

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.754
does that benefit the Republican Party?

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.822
Does the spotlight move off?

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.491
Can you maintain his vote?

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.926
You're seeing just right there

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.394
his fellow colleagues in New York

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.662
continue to criticize him,

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.130
even maybe

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.231
leadership in the House

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.233
is trying to balance this out

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.735
and about his peers in the House,

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.437
including Republicans

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.673
who at times of criticism or crisis

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.474
have not always been forthcoming

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.044
with criticism towards their colleagues,

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.979
are also starting to heat up

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.113
the rhetoric as well.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.548
It doesn't seem like

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:36.583
the scrutiny

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.384
is going to tend to leave at this.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.220
To help me understand the case,

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.621
the continuing investigation

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.423
of Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez,

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.791
you know, she went to the Met Gala.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:45.592
She wore that dress.

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:46.459
She had hair and makeup

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.061
it was all provided for her.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.529
She says she made the reimbursements

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:50.463
for it after the fact.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.365
But the Ethics Committee says

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.166
if not for the

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:54.634
opening the

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.101
review, it

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.502
appears she may not have paid

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.604
for several thousand dollars

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:58.171
worth of goods

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.072
and service provided to her.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.840
So they're trying to get a timeline of

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.308
did you only make the reimbursement

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.343
when we started questioning you?

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:03.977
Is that the issue?

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:04.544
Yeah, that is

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.279
and is requirements

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.013
and strict rules

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.715
about how you accept gifts,

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:09.816
how you disclose gifts,

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.384
what you can accept.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.318
Threshold for that.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:12.885
The question is, did

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.054
she violate any of those rules?

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.589
The committee announced that it's

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:17.890
extending its investigation,

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.559
meaning it is still ongoing.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.060
So it's not going to rise

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:21.961
to the level of Jorge

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:22.829
Santo's offense

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.530
where they may push him out of the house

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.064
of the outcome

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.366
of the ethics investigation.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.668
But she could face them,

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:29.002
you know,

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:30.069
and admonishment,

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.471
as I was mentioning earlier

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.405
from the House Ethics Committee,

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.940
if she's not acted properly by her

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.074
team, says they're confident

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.175
they can answer the questions

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.310
then it will go away.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.411
But we'll say we'll stay on top

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.345
of that one as it plays out.

